+### Offset touch sensing — 16/18/19 — ported 2026-09-26
+
+The TSP block the exporter emits around one weld's touches (`AbbProgramBlocksProvider.
+build_touchsense_program_blocks`), line for line `abb_support:abb/rapid/TGS/TD05Touch.mod`:
+
+```rapid
+stTG_SubName:="TSP<weld>_full";
+TG_ReqWeldFrame \Tool:=tTG_Weld \WObj:=wobjTG_Weld;    ! localization only: the HMI clears the touch-up
+IF nTG_WeldStatus=2 GOTO abort_end;                     ! ABB only: a malformed frame, never search in it
+TG_ReqTouchSenseDo;                                     ! 16: nTG_DoTouchSense
+TG_CamClose;
+IF nTG_DoTouchSense=1 THEN
+    TG_TeachModeOn;                                     ! only with WELDER_ENABLE_FRONIUS_TEACH_MODE
+    ... bridge ...
+    MoveL <approach>, vApproach, fine, tTG_Weld \WObj:=wobjTG_Weld;
+    TG_TouchSearch <approach>, <contact>, tTG_Weld, wobjTG_Weld;   ! TG_Touch.sys
+    TG_ReqTouchSensePoint;                              ! 18: the hit, in wobjTG_Weld
+    WaitTime 0.5;
+    MoveL <approach>, vApproach, fine, tTG_Weld \WObj:=wobjTG_Weld;  ! THE return (auto return off)
+    ... one block per touch, in the project's touch-point order ...
+    TG_ReqTouchSenseEnd \WObj:=wobjTG_Weld;            ! 19: the corrected frame -> .oframe
+ENDIF
+```
+
+- `TG_TouchSearch` is the whole search: a fine move to the approach, `SearchL \Stop` up to
+  `nTG_TouchStroke` (150 mm) along approach -> contact at `nTG_TouchSpeed` (15 mm/s), a pause and
+  retry on a miss (FANUC THSR-017 parity). Speed and stroke are controller cell data, not program
+  data -- FANUC keeps them in the touch schedule. FANUC's `Search Start`/`Search End` have no
+  counterpart.
+- **The contact** is the planner's solved contact TCP (`search_contact_embedded_target`); only
+  its direction is used. Both robtargets are in the weld's CAD frame, so the direction is
+  `-snapped_axis`, the axis the HMI reads the hit along.
+- **The order of the 18s is the project's `weld_touch_points.order_index`**: the HMI fills touch
+  point N with the Nth report and has no id on the wire.
+- Preconditions: the ABB HMI Mode profile (only the HMI turns hits into an offset) and an indexed
+  weld (coordinated touch sensing is touch-sense P7). Generation refuses the rest.
+- The HMI must accept ABB touch requests (its touch-sense P4) before a cell runs one: an HMI
+  without it aborts the run at id 16.
+
