+## ABB offset touch sensing (HMI mode, indexed welds)
+
+The same touch points and touch generation produce an ABB program. The HMI still computes the
+correction from the reported hits (HMI requests 16/18/19), exactly as on FANUC. The controller side
+is `abb_support`'s resident RAPID; its reference module is `TD05Touch.mod`.
+
+- **Where it works:** a robot group on the **ABB HMI Mode** output profile, on **indexed** welds.
+  Generation refuses the others with a message:
+  - `no_hmi`: nobody would turn the hits into a correction;
+  - coordinated welds: not ported yet.
+- **What is emitted per touch:**
+  - the approach move;
+  - `TG_TouchSearch <approach>, <contact>, tTG_Weld, wobjTG_Weld;`, where FANUC has
+    `L P[..] FINE Search[+X]`;
+  - `TG_ReqTouchSensePoint;`, a 0.5 s wait, and the move back to the approach.
+
+  Around the touches, the block has:
+  - the `TSP<weld>_full` frame request;
+  - a check that ends the run on a malformed frame;
+  - `TG_ReqTouchSenseDo`, with `TG_TeachModeOn` when *Fronius Teach mode* is on;
+  - `TG_ReqTouchSenseEnd`, which writes the corrected frame.
+
+  There is no FANUC `R_TS_F` and no `Search Start`/`Search End`.
+- **The search direction** comes from the solved contact point, so it is the touch point's snapped
+  CAD axis, the axis the HMI reads the hit along. The search speed and maximum distance are
+  controller settings in `TG_Touch.sys` (15 mm/s, 150 mm), as FANUC keeps them in its touch
+  schedule.
+- **Keep ABB searches on the snapped axis.** The HMI's correction math uses only the hit's
+  coordinate along that axis. The exporter warns on a search more than 0.5° off the work
+  object's axes.
+- **The HMI must accept ABB touch requests** (its own ABB update) before a cell runs one. An HMI
+  without it aborts the run at the first touch request.
+
+Design and the offline validation (a World Zone "part" on the MONARC virtual controller, the
+exporter's own output run through the real TG cycle) are in `abb_support`
+docs/abb_touch_sense_port_v1.md §6 P5. The tracker entry is `abb_integration_plan_v1.md` D55.
+
